  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_PlacingBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Click {0} to start drawing. Then click on the map to drop points that define your space — each click adds a corner. Close the shape by clicking back on the first point.</value><comment>{0} = "Add my barrio on the map" button label in bold</comment></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_AdjustingTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Adjusting the shape</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_Adjusting_VertexMove" xml:space="preserve"><value>Drag a corner point to move it</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_Adjusting_Reposition" xml:space="preserve"><value>Drag the whole shape to reposition it</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_Adjusting_AddVertex" xml:space="preserve"><value>Click the midpoint of an edge (where the length in metres is shown) to add a new corner</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_Adjusting_DeleteVertex" xml:space="preserve"><value>Click a point to select it (it turns orange), then press Delete or Backspace to remove it</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_Adjusting_MultiSelect" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hold Shift and click points to select multiple at once, or click and drag on empty space to draw a selection rectangle</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_Adjusting_Area" xml:space="preserve"><value>The area in m² is shown in the centre and updates as you edit</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_SavingTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Saving &amp; editing later</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_SavingBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Happy with it? Hit Save. Afterwards, click your barrio on the map to see its size, then Edit to jump back into edit mode. Every save creates a history entry — use the History button to browse and restore any previous version: hit the preview button to show the version, and then save the one you want to restore. No stress, you can't break anything!</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_ZonesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stay inside the dashed zones</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_ZonesBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>The dashed areas mark the safe camping zones, protected by lightning poles. The colour of the dashes indicates the zone's sound level — from blue (quieter) to red (louder). Camping outside them is not allowed, so keep your barrio inside those boundaries.</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_OverlapsTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Overlaps? Talk it out!</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_OverlapsBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>If your barrio overlaps with another, reach out on {0} and work it out together. If there are unresolved conflicts at the end of the phase, the city planning team will sort them out.</value><comment>{0} = Discord channel link</comment></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_OverlapsDiscordChannel" xml:space="preserve"><value>Discord #city-planning</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_ColorsTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Colours &amp; sound zones</value></data>
  <data name="CityPlanning_Help_ColorsBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each barrio is coloured by its preferred sound zone (editable from your barrio page).</value></data>
